      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:3:14:11",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الْقُرْآنِ وَ الْفُرْقَانِ أَ هُمَا شَيْئَانِ أَوْ شَيْ‏ءٌ وَاحِدٌ فَقَالَ ( عليه السلام ) الْقُرْآنُ جُمْلَةُ الْكِتَابِ وَ الْفُرْقَانُ الْمُحْكَمُ الْوَاجِبُ الْعَمَلِ بِهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Sinan, or from someone else, from the one who mentioned it who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about the Quran and the Furqan, are these two different things or one thing?’ So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The Quran is the total Book, and the Furqan is the Decisive, the Obligatory to be acted with’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "11. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn Sinan or others from those whom he has mentioned (in his book) who has said the following: “Once I asked abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) whether al-Quran and al-Furqan are two different things or one thing? The Imam said, ‘Al-Quran is the name of the whole book and al-Furqan is that much that is clearly understood and is necessary to act accordingly thereby.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
